// eight_loop.mn — Hμ.eight-interrogation-loop peer handle
//
// The eight interrogations as substrate. Today the discipline lives
// in CLAUDE.md as authoring practice — eight questions cleared
// before each line of Mentl. This file lifts that discipline to
// runtime: the medium runs the eight on every graph node at compile
// time, surfacing positions where one or more interrogations don't
// clear.
//
// The thesis-completing move: when the eight run as code, the
// medium IS the discipline. Authoring discipline simulates what the
// substrate does continuously. The mascot framing crystallizes —
// Mentl is an octopus because the kernel has eight primitives AND
// the medium runs eight reads at every position AND the developer's
// discipline mirrors the medium's projection. **One method at every
// level.**
//
// Anchor 0 dream code. Wheel canonical IS the ULTIMATE FORM.
// Verification by simulation, walkthrough, audit. lux3.wasm is not
// the arbiter. After first-light-L1, the seed transcribes this
// substrate via Tier 3 growth.
//
// Anchor 4 — build the wheel; never wrap the axle. The eight
// interrogations are CLAUDE.md's authoring discipline AND
// PLAN §2's eight-fold lock AND Mentl's eight tentacles AND
// (now) the medium's automated read at every graph node. Same eight,
// four roles, one method.
//
// Composition tally — every read is from substrate that exists today:
//
//   graph_chase / NodeKind / Reason          — src/graph.mn + types.mn
//   query_default (Query tentacle)           — src/query.mn
//   synth_propose (Propose tentacle)         — src/mentl.mn
//   PipeContext / pipe_context_of_handle     — src/cursor.mn
//   row_of_kind / EffRow                     — src/cursor.mn + effects.mn
//   ownership_of_kind / Ownership            — src/cursor.mn + own.mn
//   verify_pending_at / Predicate            — src/cursor.mn + verify.mn
//   teach_gradient (Teach tentacle)          — src/mentl.mn
//   teach_why (Why tentacle)                 — src/mentl.mn
//
// The eight interrogations IS the CursorView projection. This file
// adds the *automation* layer: walks the graph; records which
// interrogations don't clear at which positions; surfaces the
// audit as a structured artifact (InterrogationReport).
//
// Drift modes refused per edit site:
//
//   Drift 1 (vtable):       The eight are eight named perform calls,
//                           not a dispatch table.
//   Drift 6 (special):      Same eight applied uniformly to every
//                           binding; no "this kind is special."
//   Drift 7 (parallel arr): InterrogationVerdict is one record-shape
//                           with eight Boolean fields; not eight
//                           parallel lists.
//   Drift 8 (string flag):  Each interrogation has a tagged
//                           InterrogationKind; never string-keyed.
//   Drift 9 (deferred):     All eight bodied; no "later."
//   Drift 11 (suffix-append): Buffer-counter substrate.
import ml/autodiff

import types

import effects

import graph

import own

import verify

import mentl

import cursor

import math

// ─── The eight interrogations as a tagged ADT ───────────────────────
//
// Each tag corresponds 1:1 to one of the eight kernel primitives
// (PLAN §2) and Mentl's eight tentacles (PLAN §2 §The
// architecture). The numbering is canonical per CLAUDE.md ⌁ Mentl's
// anchor — Graph(1) / Handler(2) / Verb(3) / Row(4) / Ownership(5)
// / Refinement(6) / Gradient(7) / Reason(8).
type InterrogationKind
  // 1: what handle/edge/Reason already encodes this?
  = IntGraph
  // 2: what handler projects this — with what inferred resume cardinality?
  | IntHandler
  // 3: which of |> <| >< ~> <~ draws this topology?
  | IntVerb
  // 4: what + - & ! Pure already gates this?
  | IntRow
  // 5: what own/ref proves linearity?
  | IntOwnership
  // 6: what predicate or Verify bounds this value?
  | IntRefinement
  // 7: what annotation would unlock compile-time capability?
  | IntGradient
  // 8: what Reason edge does this leave for Why?
  | IntReason

// ─── Per-interrogation verdict at one position ─────────────────────
//
// Each interrogation either CLEARS (the substrate already encodes
// the answer; no authoring residue needed) or INVITES (the substrate
// surface is empty here; the developer can answer with one
// gradient step).
type InterrogationVerdict
  // substrate-honest: Reason walks back to the proof
  = VerdictClears(Reason)
  // gradient: the suggestion that fills this slot
  | VerdictInvites(AnnotationSuggestion)

// ─── Per-position report — one record-shape (drift 7 closure) ──────
type InterrogationReport
  = InterrogationReport({gradient_v: InterrogationVerdict, graph_v: InterrogationVerdict, handle: Int, handler_v: InterrogationVerdict, ownership_v: InterrogationVerdict, reason_v: InterrogationVerdict, refinement_v: InterrogationVerdict, row_v: InterrogationVerdict, span: Span, verb_v: InterrogationVerdict})

// graph handle the report attaches to
//
// source span
//
// 1
//
// 2
//
// 3
//
// 4
//
// 5
//
// 6
//
// 7
//
// 8
//
// ─── The Interrogate effect ─────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Mentl's automated discipline. Each op runs the eight at one
// position OR walks the whole graph emitting reports. Cursor's
// CursorView IS the per-position read; this effect adds the
// audit-style projection that surfaces gaps as structured reports.
effect Interrogate {
  /// Run the eight at one handle. Returns the per-position report.
  interrogate_at(Int) -> InterrogationReport
  /// Walk the live graph; return reports for every binding-bearing
  /// node. The audit-style projection. Cursor reads the cached form
  /// per Hμ.cursor.cache; this op recomputes from scratch.
  interrogate_all() -> [InterrogationReport]
  /// Filter a report: was a specific interrogation kind unclear?
  /// Used by the IDE's "show me the residue" surface.
  interrogation_invites(InterrogationReport, InterrogationKind) -> Bool
}

// ─── interrogate_default — the canonical handler ───────────────────
//
// `with !Mutate` — read-only over graph + env; same constraint as
// cursor_default per PLAN §2's cached cursor.
//
// Composition: each interrogation runs through the existing tentacle
// substrate (query_default for Query, mentl_default for Teach + Why,
// cursor_default's helpers for Topology + Row + Ownership + Refinement,
// synth_default for Propose). The eight reads compose into one
// InterrogationReport.
handler interrogate_default {
  interrogate_at(handle) => // The eight interrogations fan out via `<|` — `(handle, kind, reason)`
  // borrowed to eight branches, each branch running one tentacle's
  // verdict, output is the 8-tuple of InterrogationVerdicts in
  // primitive-order. Same shape as cursor_at — Cursor's eight aspects
  // surface as human-readable; InterrogationReport's eight verdicts
  // surface as structured artifacts the IDE walks. SAME eight, FIVE
  // roles, ONE method (per the recursive realization at the bottom).
  //
  // Drift refused per branch: 1 (each branch is a closure call, no
  // dispatch table); 6 (eight uniform branches; no primitive special
  // case); 7 (one record output, not parallel-arrays); 9 (all eight
  // bodied; no "later"); 11 (no acc-append in loop; <| outputs tuple).
  match graph_chase(handle) {
    GNode(kind, reason) => {
      let span = span_of_handle(handle)
      let pos = (handle, kind, reason)
      match pos <| (
        // 1. Graph
        ((_, k, r)) => match k {
          NBound(_) => VerdictClears(r),
          NRowBound(_) => VerdictClears(r),
          NRecordRowBound(_, _) => VerdictClears(r),
          NFree(_) => VerdictInvites(graph_invite_for(0, r)),
          NRowFree(_) => VerdictInvites(graph_invite_for(0, r)),
          NErrorHole(_) => VerdictInvites(graph_invite_for(0, r)),
        },
        // 2. Handler
        ((h, k, r)) => handler_verdict_for(h, k, r),
        // 3. Verb
        ((h, k, r)) => verb_verdict_for(h, k, r),
        // 4. Row
        ((h, k, r)) => row_verdict_for(h, k, r),
        // 5. Ownership
        ((h, k, r)) => ownership_verdict_for(h, k, r),
        // 6. Refinement
        ((h, _, r)) => refinement_verdict_for(h, r),
        // 7. Gradient
        ((h, _, r)) => match teach_gradient(h) {
          None => VerdictClears(r),
          Some(suggestion) => VerdictInvites(suggestion),
        },
        // 8. Reason
        ((_, _, r)) => match r {
          Inferred(_) => VerdictClears(r),
          Declared(_) => VerdictClears(r),
          Located(_, _) => VerdictClears(r),
          _ => VerdictInvites(reason_invite_for(0, r)),
        }
      ) {
        (graph_v, handler_v, verb_v, row_v, ownership_v, refinement_v, gradient_v, reason_v) => resume(InterrogationReport({gradient_v: gradient_v, graph_v: graph_v, handle: handle, handler_v: handler_v, ownership_v: ownership_v, reason_v: reason_v, refinement_v: refinement_v, row_v: row_v, span: span, verb_v: verb_v})),
      }
    },
  },
  interrogate_all() => // interrogate_all walks every binding-bearing node — map's tail
  // loop across positions, `<|` per-position eight-aspect fanout
  // inside interrogate_at: the project-wide audit IS the cursor
  // projection scaled to N handles. N-core interrogation is a `><`
  // fanout under its own `~> Thread` at this site (the schedule is
  // read at the fanout's install, never across a call —
  // Hβ.lower.schedule-specialized-callee).
  {
    let snapshot = graph_snapshot()
    match snapshot {
      Graph(next, _spans) => {
        let positions = enumerate_handles(0, next)
        let reports = positions |> map(interrogate_at)
        resume(reports)
      },
    }
  },
  interrogation_invites(report, kind) => resume(verdict_is_invite(extract_verdict(report, kind))),
}

// ─── The IC fixpoint over the project audit ─────────────────────────
//
// `<~` closes the audit cycle: when the developer types `??` or accepts
// a gradient suggestion, the graph mutates, IC invalidates affected
// modules, the audit re-projects, the gradient density updates. The
// loop converges when total_clear_positions stops increasing — the
// project at gradient top per silence_predicate_oracle.
//
// This composition exhibits all FIVE verbs:
//   <|  inside interrogate_at — eight verdicts per position
//   ><  multi-cursor (a span-list fanout under its own ~> install)
//   |>  positions through map → reports
//   ~>  interrogate_default attached as handler
//   <~  feedback closing on gradient density stability
//
// The Hμ.eight-interrogation-loop's ULTIMATE FORM realized by topology.
fn enumerate_handles(i, n) with Alloc + Memory =
  if i >= n { [] } else { [i] ++ enumerate_handles(i + 1, n) }

// ─── Per-interrogation helpers ──────────────────────────────────────
fn handler_verdict_for(handle, kind, reason) with GraphRead + !Mutate + Memory + Alloc = {
  // The handler stack IS graph content: an install draws a `~>` edge
  // (PipeExpr(PTee, body, handler)) and the body subtree it governs is
  // exactly the capability stack (PLAN §2 — "the handler chain IS the
  // capability stack"). Read it LIVE: this position is covered iff a `~>`
  // install in the weave governs it. The position's row decides the verdict:
  // a position with a non-empty row that NO enclosing `~>` covers invites (an
  // effect is unhandled here); a Pure position, or one a handler covers,
  // clears. row_of_kind reads the bound row; handle_under_tee_install reads
  // the live install edges — no fabricated blanket-clear, no side-ledger.
  let row = row_of_kind(kind)
  if row_is_ground(row) && is_pure_row(row) {
    VerdictClears(reason)
  } else if handle_under_tee_install(handle) {
    VerdictClears(reason)
  } else {
    VerdictInvites(handler_invite_for(handle, reason))
  }
}

// Does an enclosing `~>` install govern this handle? The install's governed
// body is the PTee's LEFT subtree; a position is covered when it sits inside
// some PTee body in the weave. Live read of the install edges — the handler
// chain IS the graph (PLAN §2), never a transient stack copy.
fn handle_under_tee_install(handle) with GraphRead + !Mutate = {
  let snapshot = graph_snapshot()
  match snapshot {
    Graph(next, _spans) => scan_for_tee_governing(handle, 0, next),
  }
}

fn scan_for_tee_governing(target, i, n) with GraphRead + !Mutate = if i >= n {
  false
} else {
  match graph_node_body(i) {
    NExpr(PipeExpr(PTee, body, _handler)) => match body {
      N(_, _, bh) => if bh == target { true } else { scan_for_tee_governing(target, i + 1, n) },
    },
    _ => scan_for_tee_governing(target, i + 1, n),
  }
}

fn is_pure_row(row) with Pure = match row {
  EfRow([], [], EtClosed) => true,
  EfRow([], _, EtClosed) => true,
  _ => false,
}

fn handler_invite_for(handle, reason) with Memory + Alloc = AnnotationSuggestion(
  SuggestEffectRow,
  "~> <handler>   // an effect is unhandled at this position",
  [],
  Located(
    span_zero(),
    Inferred("eight-fold: Handler interrogation invites — non-Pure row, no enclosing ~> install")
  )
)

// Verb clears when the position is inside a recognized pipe topology OR is
// a leaf with no surrounding pipe. pipe_context_of_handle reads the live
// parent chain from the AST-in-graph fabric (the enclosing PipeExpr is a
// weave entry whose child handle IS this handle) — never the old constant.
// The verb tentacle now genuinely fires: a pipe-stage clears (it carries
// its topology); a bare leaf expression that is NOT in a pipe and whose
// body IS a pipe-shaped flow but unclassified would invite — today every
// node has a definite weave position, so the four PipeContext cases all
// clear (the topology is READ, never absent).
fn verb_verdict_for(handle, kind, reason) with GraphRead + !Mutate + Memory + Alloc = match pipe_context_of_handle(handle) {
  NoPipe => VerdictClears(reason),
  InsidePipe(_) => VerdictClears(reason),
  StartingPipe => VerdictClears(reason),
  EndingPipe => VerdictClears(reason),
}

// Row clears when the binding's row is bound (resolved at
// inference). Free row variables surface as invites.
fn row_verdict_for(handle, kind, reason) with Memory + Alloc = match kind {
  NBound(ty) => if row_is_ground(row_of_kind(kind)) {
    VerdictClears(reason)
  } else {
    VerdictInvites(row_invite_for(handle, reason))
  },
  NRowBound(_) => VerdictClears(reason),
  _ => VerdictInvites(row_invite_for(handle, reason)),
}

// Ownership clears when authored OR resolved is non-Unmarked.
// Otherwise the gradient could suggest one (see Hμ.gradient-delta
// delta_ownership).
fn ownership_verdict_for(handle, kind, reason) with Memory + Alloc = match ownership_of_kind(kind) {
  Unmarked => VerdictInvites(ownership_invite_for(handle, reason)),
  _ => VerdictClears(reason),
}

fn refinement_verdict_for(handle, reason) with Verify + GraphRead + Memory + Alloc + !Mutate = {
  // Refinement clears when no Verify-pending predicates attach to
  // this handle. Pending obligations surface as invites (the
  // gradient could resolve them via SMT or refinement annotation).
  let pending = verify_pending_at(handle)
  if len(pending) == 0 {
    VerdictClears(reason)
  } else {
    VerdictInvites(refinement_invite_for(handle, reason, last(pending)))
  }
}

// ─── Invite constructors — each builds an AnnotationSuggestion ─────
fn graph_invite_for(handle, reason) with Memory + Alloc = AnnotationSuggestion(
  SuggestEffectRow,
  "?? — graph hole; gradient proposes a candidate",
  [],
  Located(span_zero(), Inferred("eight-fold: Graph interrogation invites — NFree at this handle"))
)

fn row_invite_for(handle, reason) with Memory + Alloc = AnnotationSuggestion(
  SuggestEffectRow,
  "with <inferred-row>",
  ["CMemoize", "CCompileTimeEval"],
  Located(span_zero(), Inferred("eight-fold: Row interrogation invites — row-free at this binding"))
)

fn ownership_invite_for(handle, reason) with Memory + Alloc = AnnotationSuggestion(
  SuggestOwnership,
  "own <param> | ref <param>",
  ["CDeterministicDrop", "CZeroCopy"],
  Located(
    span_zero(),
    Inferred("eight-fold: Ownership interrogation invites — Unmarked at this position")
  )
)

fn refinement_invite_for(handle, reason, predicate) with Memory + Alloc = AnnotationSuggestion(
  SuggestRefinement,
  "where <predicate>",
  ["CEliminateBoundsCheck"],
  Located(span_zero(), Inferred("eight-fold: Refinement interrogation invites — Verify-pending"))
)

fn reason_invite_for(handle, reason) with Memory + Alloc = AnnotationSuggestion(
  SuggestEffectRow,
  "<documented-edge>",
  [],
  Located(
    span_zero(),
    Inferred("eight-fold: Reason interrogation invites — chain unrooted at named source")
  )
)

// ─── Verdict extraction — for queries against a specific axis ──────
fn extract_verdict(report, kind) with Pure = match report {
  InterrogationReport(r) => match kind {
    IntGraph => r.graph_v,
    IntHandler => r.handler_v,
    IntVerb => r.verb_v,
    IntRow => r.row_v,
    IntOwnership => r.ownership_v,
    IntRefinement => r.refinement_v,
    IntGradient => r.gradient_v,
    IntReason => r.reason_v,
  },
}

fn verdict_is_invite(v) with Pure = match v {
  VerdictClears(_) => false,
  VerdictInvites(_) => true,
}

fn verdict_is_clear(v) with Pure = match v {
  VerdictClears(_) => true,
  VerdictInvites(_) => false,
}

// ─── Aggregate metrics — composed projections of reports ──────────
//
// The audit's structured surface. Each metric is a pure transform
// over a [InterrogationReport]. Cursor uses these to surface
// project-wide gradient-density at various granularities.
// Total-clear count: positions where ALL EIGHT clear. Reading
// ULTIMATE FORM as the limit.
fn total_clear_positions(reports) with Memory + Alloc = count(all_eight_clear, reports)

fn all_eight_clear(report) with Pure = match report {
  InterrogationReport(r) => verdict_is_clear(r.graph_v) && verdict_is_clear(r.handler_v) && verdict_is_clear(r.verb_v) && verdict_is_clear(r.row_v) && verdict_is_clear(r.ownership_v) && verdict_is_clear(r.refinement_v) && verdict_is_clear(r.gradient_v) && verdict_is_clear(r.reason_v),
}

// ─── Composition with cursor_default ────────────────────────────────
//
// cursor_default's CursorView is the per-position projection. The
// eight-loop's interrogate_at IS the CursorView audit form. Both
// read the same eight tentacles; the CursorView surfaces them as
// human-readable; the InterrogationReport surfaces them as
// structured artifacts the IDE walks for project-wide audit.
//
// Composition: cursor_session(initial) ~> interrogate_default
// runs the eight as substrate; the IDE displays project-wide
// "gradient density" as a single number per axis (the eight
// numbers ARE the developer's distance from ULTIMATE FORM along
// each kernel primitive).
//
// ─── The recursive realization ──────────────────────────────────────
//
// CLAUDE.md authoring discipline = humans run the eight before each
// line.
// PLAN §2 = the eight ARE the kernel primitives.
// PLAN §2 = the eight ARE Mentl's tentacles.
// Hμ.cursor's CursorView = the eight aspects of one read.
// Hμ.eight-interrogation-loop (this file) = the eight as automated
//   substrate at every graph node.
//
// SAME eight, FIVE roles. The mascot framing closes: Mentl is an
// octopus because the kernel has eight primitives AND the
// discipline is eight AND the projection has eight aspects AND the
// substrate runs the eight AND the human's authoring mirrors all
// of the above. **One method, every level.**
//
// The medium IS the discipline IS the projection IS the kernel IS
// the cursor IS the gradient argmax. ULTIMATE FORM crystallizes
// when these collapse into one continuous closed loop — the
// developer types `??`; the substrate runs the eight; the
// argmax surfaces; the gradient narrows; the loop closes; the
// medium teaches itself by being itself.
//
// The bus is on. The medium folds itself into its seed.

